.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH kakashi-converge 1  "converge " 
.SH NAME
kakashi\-converge \- Run one convergence iteration and append it to the ledger (§38, §39)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBkakashi converge\fR [\fB\-\-reference\-corpus\fR] [\fB\-\-state\fR] [\fB\-\-format\fR] [\fB\-\-replica\-corpus\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIREFERENCE\fR> <\fIREPLICA\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run one convergence iteration and append it to the ledger (§38, §39)
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-reference\-corpus\fR \fI<REFERENCE_CORPUS>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-state\fR \fI<STATE>\fR [default: .]
Directory containing (or to contain) the `.kakashi/` state directory (§34)
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<FORMAT>\fR [default: human]

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-replica\-corpus\fR \fI<REPLICA_CORPUS>\fR

.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIREFERENCE\fR>

.TP
<\fIREPLICA\fR>

